  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Light of wavelength <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda\"></span> is incident on a slit of width b and forms a diffraction pattern. The central maximum has a width of θ radians. The wavelength of the light is now changed to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2}{3}\\lambda\"></span> and the slit width is changed to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{6}\"></span>b.</p>\n<p>What is the angle between the first diffraction minimum and the point of maximum intensity?<br/><br/></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{4}\"></span>θ</li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2}\"></span>θ</li><li data-label=\"C\">2θ</li><li data-label=\"D\">4θ</li></ol>"
